        "type": "4-Mark Inference",
        "marks": 4,
        "targetMins": 6,
        "questionText": "Give two things you can infer from Source A about communist supply lines along the Ho Chi Minh Trail in 1965.",
        "stimulus": [],
        "sourceExtract": "<div style=\"font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 6px; font-weight: 600;\">Source A: From an American military intelligence report on communist logistics in South Vietnam, 1965.</div><div>\"The flow of communist troops and war supplies along the Ho Chi Minh Trail has escalated sharply over the past year. Porters and supply convoys move under dense double-canopy jungle that completely conceals them from our reconnaissance aircraft. They transport mortars, ammunition, and medical supplies using reinforced bicycles and pack animals, moving through Laos directly into South Vietnam. Despite thousands of air strikes, the supply route remains unbroken.\"</div>",
        "modelAnswer": "<strong>Sample Acceptable Inferences (communist supply lines along the Ho Chi Minh Trail in 1965):</strong>\n• <strong>Inference 1:</strong> The natural jungle terrain effectively hid communist troop movements and supplies from American air detection.\n  - <em>Detail from source:</em> \"Porters and supply convoys move under dense double-canopy jungle that completely conceals them from our reconnaissance aircraft.\"\n\n• <strong>Inference 2:</strong> US air strikes were unable to stop the sharp increase in supplies moving into South Vietnam.\n  - <em>Detail from source:</em> \"The flow of communist troops and war supplies along the Ho Chi Minh Trail has escalated sharply... Despite thousands of air strikes, the supply route remains unbroken.\"",
