        "sourceExtract": "<div style=\"font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 6px; font-weight: 600;\">Source A: From a letter written by a US soldier to his family, describing his experiences on a Search and Destroy mission in South Vietnam, 1967.</div><div>We patrol through this thick jungle for days, carrying 60 pounds of gear in 100-degree heat. You can't see the enemy, but you know they are watching. Suddenly, a tripwire is hit and a homemade booby trap goes off, killing two of our buddies. There are no North Vietnamese soldiers to shoot back at, just empty jungle and suspicious villagers who refuse to speak to us. Out of frustration and fear, our guys burned down their thatch huts. We are fighting a shadow, and it is driving us crazy.</div>",
